From: ClockworkPi local kernel review
Subject: [PATCH] video: kd027: restore vendor serial data setup before clock pulse

The DRM-panel conversion in cpi3-006 moved the falling SCK edge before
the SDA update. Clockwork's vendor driver drives SDA while SCK is high,
then pulses SCK low and high. The conversion therefore stopped providing
the same data setup time before the falling edge.

Restore the vendor's order and add a one-microsecond setup interval.
Keep the existing low/high hold delays, register bytes and chip select
framing. This makes each transmitted bit stable before either edge,
without assuming an undocumented KD027 sampling edge.

test-003 still flickers and shows more white horizontal lines than
test-002 according to the user's hardware report. This patch corrects
an observed waveform difference; it does not establish that serial
sampling is the cause of that display corruption. Keep test-003's
pixel clock and mode unchanged to isolate this test.

Reference: clockworkpi/Kernel CPI3_linux_4.20/cpi3_linux_4_20_1902.patch,
kd027_write_lcd().
https://github.com/clockworkpi/Kernel/blob/master/CPI3_linux_4.20/cpi3_linux_4_20_1902.patch

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/kd027_lcd.c b/drivers/video/backlight/kd027_lcd.c
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/kd027_lcd.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/kd027_lcd.c
@@ -34,8 +34,10 @@
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+		/* Match the vendor waveform: data precedes both clock edges. */
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lcd->sda, !!(data & 0x80));
+		udelay(1);
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lcd->sck, 0);
-		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lcd->sda, !!(data & 0x80));
 		udelay(1);
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lcd->sck, 1);
 		udelay(1);
